            <ArticleTitle>Anticoagulant Effects of Arginine-Containing Peptides of the Glyproline Family (His-Phe-Arg-Trp-Pro-Gly-Pro and Thr-Lys-Pro-Arg-Pro-Gly-Pro) Revealed by Thromboelastography.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>170-172</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s10517-017-3950-4</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Thromboelastography revealed anticoagulant effects of 3 glyproline oligopeptides (in various concentrations): His-Phe-Arg-Trp-Pro-Gly-Pro, Thr-Lys-Pro-Arg-Pro-Gly-Pro (Selank), and Pro-Gly-Pro. The parameters R, K, MA, S, TMA, and J changed to hypocoagulation direction in comparison to the control. At this, Selank demonstrated the maximal anticoagulation potency.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
